Z||000000||hugh||07-22-2001||09:08 AM||||We all make decisions based on what we perceive to be our true world.We get input from family,friends,associates,television,newspapers,etc.I can picture us as individually  being enveloped in a huge bubble and making contact with other bubble's information  as we float through our lives.(wierd huh?).It's almost like those kids amusements at fairs that has a blowup enclosure with a lot of loose balls.The balls get moved around,but still only come into contact with a limited number of other balls.<BR>Another thought;<BR> Right now you are obviously at your computer.Have you ever thought about what is happening to others at this exact moment?Somewhere,as you read this,there is someone who is going through excruciating pain,and there is someone that is experiencing tremendous pleasure.Someone is being born,someone is dying,someone is happy,someone is sad.You will see in the news about these things,or hear about them from somewhere else,but it will be after the fact.They are happening right now! <BR>   I'm done for now. ||||reg||1
